{
  "requirement": "`habeas mdbook` MUST NOT generate per-test coverage subchapters or captured-source\npages under the execution-coverage chapter of\n{cite}`requirements.test-coverage.index`. File-notes pages supporting coverage\ngap explanations under {cite}`requirements.test-coverage.index.file_map.notes`\nMUST remain available.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The tests adequately check both obligations of `requirements.test-coverage.index.details`. Three tests in `src/execution_coverage/book.rs` carry the {test} reference. I did not read the `record` and `fixture` helpers or the implementation, and the judgment rests on the test sources supplied.\n\n**1. MUST NOT generate per-test coverage subchapters or captured-source pages under the execution-coverage chapter.**\n- `mod[tests]/fn[book_ignores_saved_measurements_and_preserves_artifacts]` records a saved attempt with the `record` helper. The attempt has a test name, a profraw file and line data. The test then populates the book and requires the chapters to be identical to those of a book populated with no saved attempt.\n- The same test requires the full chapter-name list to be exactly `[\"Documented coverage gaps\", \"File notes: code.rs\"]`. A per-test subchapter or a captured-source page would add a chapter and fail this assertion.\n- For every chapter it asserts three things. The saved test name does not appear in the content. There is no `<select`. The path does not contain `-source`.\n- It repeats the chapter comparison with corrupt attempt metadata (`invalid metadata` and `{}`), so the result does not depend on valid saved data.\n- It asserts that the overview omits `Captured source`, `Test runs and provenance`, `selected test attempts` and `Line coverage:`.\n- `generated_reports_inherit_the_requirements_index_hierarchy` iterates over every sub-item of the coverage chapter. It requires each to be a file-notes-style page with the expected numbering and `../coverage.html` links. It also checks `parent.sub_items.len() == 2`. No extra per-test pages appear in either the numbered or unnumbered variant.\n- In `documented_items_are_counted_once_with_browsable_directory_and_file_groups`, the count of pages named `File notes:` is exactly 5. The pages generated for the documented files are therefore the only per-file pages.\n\n**2. File-notes pages MUST remain available.**\n- `documented_items_are_counted_once_with_browsable_directory_and_file_groups` checks each documented file as follows:\n  - A chapter named `File notes: {file}` exists.\n  - Its path equals `notes::path(...)`.\n  - Its content contains `File: <code>{file}</code>`.\n  - Its anchors `coverage-note-{ordinal}` exist.\n  - The file card links to those anchors.\n- Together with the count of 5, this shows the notes pages exist and are reachable.\n- `book_ignores_saved_measurements_and_preserves_artifacts` shows the `File notes: code.rs` page survives alongside saved measurements.\n\n**Gaps.** I found no gap. Marking is present, and the assertions enforce both the negative and the positive obligation. There is no acknowledged {fixme}, and none is needed.",
